ay $x=1$.\n\n$f(1) = 2^6 + 0^5 + 2^4 + 0^3 + 2^2 + 0 + 1 = 64 + 16 + 4 + 1 = 85$.\n\n$f(-1) = 0^6 + (-2)^5 + 0^4 + (-2)^3 + 0^2 + (-2) + 1 = 0 - 32 + 0 - 8 + 0 - 2 + 1 = -41$.\n\n$g(1) = f(1) - f(-1) = 85 - (-41) = 126$.\n\n$g(1) = 14 \\cdot 1 + 70 \\cdot 1 + 42 \\cdot 1 = 14 + 70 + 42 = 126$. ✓\n\nLet me check $x=2$:\n\n$f(2) = 3^6 + 1^5 + 3^4 + 1^3 + 3^2 + 1 + 1 = 729 + 1 + 81 + 1 + 9 + 1 + 1 = 823$.\n\n$f(-2) = (-1)^6 + (-3)^5 + (-1)^4 + (-3)^3 + (-1)^2 + (-3) + 1 = 1 - 243 + 1 - 27 + 1 - 3 + 1 = -269$.\n\n$g(2) = 823 - (-269) = 1092$.\n\n$g(2) = 14 \\cdot 32 + 70 \\cdot 8 + 42 \\cdot 2 = 448 + 560 + 84 = 1092$. ✓\n\nSo $g(x) = 14x^5 + 70x^3 + 42x$ is confirmed.\n\nNow $S = \\sum_{j=1}^{126} j \\cdot g(j) = \\sum_{j=1}^{126} (14j^6 + 70j^4 + 42j^2)$.\n\n$= 14 \\sum j^6 + 70 \\sum j^4 + 42 \\sum j^2$.\n\nI've computed:\n- $14 \\sum j^6 \\mod 1000 = 714$\n- $70 \\sum j^4 \\mod 1000 = 570$\n- $42 \\sum j^2 \\mod 1000 = 542$\n\nTotal: $714 + 570 + 542 = 1826 \\equiv 826 \\pmod{1000}$.\n\nThe answer is $\\boxed{826}$.\n\nWait, I should double-check the intermediate modular computations more carefully since these are large products.\n\n$\\sum j^2 = 674751$. Let me verify: $126 \\cdot 127 \\cdot 253 / 6$. $126/6 = 21$. $21 \\cdot 127 = 2667$. $2667 \\cdot 253 = 2667 \\cdot 250 + 2667 \\cdot 3 = 666750 + 8001 = 674751$. ✓\n\n$42 \\times 674751$: I need mod 1000. $674751 \\mod 1000 = 751$. $42 \\times 751 = 31542$. $\\mod 1000 = 542$. ✓\n\n$\\sum j^4 = 6478284351$. $\\mod 1000 = 351$. $70 \\times 351 = 24570$. $\\mod 1000 = 570$. ✓\n\n$\\sum j^6 = 96393 \\times 768297607$. $\\mod 1000$: $393 \\times 607 = 238551$. $\\mod 1000 = 551$. $14 \\times 551 = 7714$. $\\mod 1000 = 714$. ✓\n\n$714 + 570 + 542 = 1826$. $1826 \\mod 1000 = 826$.\n\nThe answer is $826$.\n\nActually, let me be extra careful and recompute $\\sum j^6 \\mod 1000$ using a different decomposition to cross-check.\n\n$\\sum j^6 = \\frac{4048506 \\times 768297607}{42}$.\n\nI need this mod 1000. But division by 42 in modular arithmetic is tricky since $\\gcd(42, 1000) = 2 \\neq 1$. So I can't just compute $4048506 \\times 768297607 \\mod 1000$ and divide by 42.\n\nInstead, I computed $4048506 / 42 = 96393$ exactly (integer), then $96393 \\times 768297607 \\mod 1000 = 393 \\times 607 \\mod 1000 = 551$.\n\nLet me verify $4048506 / 42 = 96393$: $42 \\times 96393 = 42 \\times 96000 + 42 \\times 393 = 4032000 + 16506 = 4048506$. ✓\n\nSo $\\sum j^6 \\mod 1000 = 551$.\n\n$14 \\times 551 = 7714$, $\\mod 1000 = 714$. ✓\n\nSo the final answer is $826$.\n\nLet me also verify $\\sum j^4 \\mod 1000$ differently.\n\n$\\sum j^4 = \\frac{4048506 \\times 48005}{30}$. $4048506 / 6 = 674751$. $674751 \\times 48005 / 5 = 674751 \\times 9601 = 6478284351$. $\\mod 1000 = 351$. $70 \\times 351 = 24570$, $\\mod 1000 = 570$. ✓\n\nEverything checks out. The answer is $\\boxed{826}$.", "tool_calls": [], "created_at": 1786760621}
